A||||5||BAM-BAM||Header question????||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-19-2001||06:35 AM||||Which is the better way to go? Fiero Store Sprint headers? FOCOA headers? Westco headers? or just the good ol' port and polish on the stock manifolds? I really want to know where the better power gain for the money lies. After that it's all for appearence sake. TIA.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>  <BR>  <BR> <BR> <P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||5
Z||000001||skitime||04-19-2001||08:00 AM||||The best power gain for the money is ported stock manifolds.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||04-19-2001||08:02 AM||||if you want high end HP get headers.. or if your running a S/C or nitrous get headers. if you want a quick off the line car with only basic mods, port the stock units... and save the $ for gas... $500 is a LOT of gas...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg</A> <P>the 11lbft loss of torque just killed my car... but on nitrous i gained nearly 60lbft with no jet change. from 253 to 310lbft. theres deffinatly a trade off though. cwestco fit great and look D@MN cool too... ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-19-2001||10:21 AM||||The only advantage the Sprints or Chris West's shorty's have over the stock ported manifolds is they won't crack. (and looks) Even after having the stocks ported and the welds fixed, they can still crack. I believe that the Sprints/CW Shorty's have slightly better flow but not enough to make a  difference. I have Sprints on my car because I bought them when they first came out in 1995.(for about $120 less than they are now!) Which was way before the resources that we have today. I have been happy with them and thet still look like new.<BR>(They came jet coated) Some folks have said that on the 3.1L or 3.4L they make a bigger difference but I have never seen any "real" data. Maybe we should get 1FST2M6 a car and all of the manifolds/headers available so we can have a true reading of which is better or if their is any difference at all.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||04-19-2001||01:00 PM||||  Whatever I get or use will be on my "NEW" 3.4L. I was thinking about CW's shorty's for appearence, but the Sprint's come hot coated. Do they require a speacial crossover on any of the afore mentined styles? I need all the info I can get in order to make my best decision. Thanks and TIA<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||6
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||04-19-2001||10:11 PM||||The Sorints bolt right up and the larger ones<BR>come with a crossover.<BR>I would suggest using the Jet Hot on whatever<BR>one you get, the Fiero's engine compartment<BR>isn't a cool place. :-)<BR>A guy in my club has a 3.1 and the F.O.C.O.A.<BR>headers and says the car really comes alive in the top end.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
